            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Apple 'way behind' on AI. But maybe that's not a bad thing right now.",
            "description": "<p>As Apple (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL\">AAPL</a>) advertises its latest generation of devices \u2014 namely the <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/apple-debuts-superthin-iphone-air-alongside-iphone-17-and-iphone-17-pro-181527722.html\">iPhone 17 and slim iPhone Air </a>\u2014 around its artificial intelligence features, does this position it as a growth stock?</p>\n<p>Ritholtz Wealth Management chief market strategist Callie Cox weighs in on Apple's status as a growth stock option and whether the company is <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/iphone-underwhelms-wall-street-apple-141612068.html\">falling behind on its AI promises.</a></p>\n<p>Also catch Yahoo Finance's<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/t-ceo-highlights-challenges-spacex-205128589.html\"> full interview </a>with AT&T (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/T\">T</a>) CEO John Stankey, where he comments on the release of the iPhone 17.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
